% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The fields of a powered product (the listing format)
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
"power source" reading "ac" shows a powered product,
    as stated in the other products listing format, confer "Power Source (14 listings: \"AC\", \"DC\", \"Battery\", \"Electric\")".
"power source" reading "dc" shows a powered product,
    as stated in the other products listing format, confer "Power Source (14 listings: \"AC\", \"DC\", \"Battery\", \"Electric\")".
"power source" reading "battery" shows a powered product,
    as stated in the other products listing format, confer "Power Source (14 listings: \"AC\", \"DC\", \"Battery\", \"Electric\")".
"power source" reading "electric" shows a powered product,
    as stated in the other products listing format, confer "Power Source (14 listings: \"AC\", \"DC\", \"Battery\", \"Electric\")".
"is electric" reading "lithium battery" shows a powered product,
    as stated in the other products listing format, confer "Is Electric (12: \"No Battery\", \"Lithium Battery\", \"Button Battery\")".
"is electric" reading "button battery" shows a powered product,
    as stated in the other products listing format, confer "Is Electric (12: \"No Battery\", \"Lithium Battery\", \"Button Battery\")".
"electronic" reading "yes" shows a powered product,
    as stated in the other products listing format, confer "Electronic (12: \"Yes\" or \"No\")".
"is smart device" reading "yes" shows a powered product,
    as stated in the other products listing format, confer "Is Smart Device (11)".

% a field whose every value, but a word for no value, shows a powered product
"voltage" is a field of a powered product,
    as stated in the other products listing format, confer "Voltage (23)".
"power (w)" is a field of a powered product,
    as stated in the other products listing format, confer "Power (W) (7)".

% the words for no value, as the listings write them
"none" is a word for no value,
    as stated in the other products listing format, confer "Certification (88: \"CE\", \"CE,FCC,RoHS\", \"None\")".
"no" is a word for no value,
    as stated in the other products listing format, confer "Electronic (12: \"Yes\" or \"No\")".

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The rules
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
rule claim_by_name with provenance the other products listing format,
        confer "A listing offers one finished product for sale":
a good is claimed to belong to a kind
    if the good is called a name
    and the name is a word for an article of the kind.

rule claim_by_field with provenance the other products listing format,
        confer "The fields that describe what the product is:":
a good is claimed to belong to a kind
    if the field a field of the good reads a value
    and the field is a field that names the product
    and the value is a word for an article of the kind.

% A category is weak evidence: no claim when an earlier background gave the
% good a kind or a principal use, or when the good is also in a category of
% goods of a modelled chapter.
rule claim_by_category with provenance the other products listing format,
        confer "The shop's first category is, for example:":
a good is claimed to belong to a kind
    if the good is in the shop category a category
    and the category is a shop category of articles of the kind
    and it is not the case that
        the kind of the good is an other kind
    and it is not the case that
        the principal use of the good is a use
    and it is not the case that
        the good is in the shop category an other category
        and the other category is a shop category of goods of a modelled chapter.

% A word or a category of the good names an article of another chapter.
rule other_chapter_by_name with provenance the other products listing format,
        confer "A listing offers one finished product for sale":
a good has a word of goods of another chapter
    if the good is called a name
    and the name is a word for an article of a kind.
rule other_chapter_by_field with provenance the other products listing format,
        confer "The fields that describe what the product is:":
a good has a word of goods of another chapter
    if the field a field of the good reads a value
    and the field is a field that names the product
    and the value is a word for an article of a kind.
rule other_chapter_by_category with provenance the other products listing format,
        confer "The shop's first category is, for example:":
a good has a word of goods of another chapter
    if the good is in the shop category a category
    and the category is a shop category of articles of a kind.

% A powered product: a claim to the machinery of Section XVI, unless a word
% or a category already names the other chapter, an earlier background gave
% the good a kind, or the good is in a category of toys or watches.
rule claim_by_power_field with provenance the other products listing format,
        confer "Fields of a powered product:":
a good is claimed to belong to machinery of section XVI
    if the field a field of the good reads a value
    and the field reading the value shows a powered product
    and it is not the case that
        the good has a word of goods of another chapter
    and it is not the case that
        the kind of the good is a kind
    and it is not the case that
        the good is in the shop category a category
        and the category is a shop category of goods of a modelled chapter.

rule claim_by_power_value with provenance the other products listing format,
        confer "Fields of a powered product:":
a good is claimed to belong to machinery of section XVI
    if the field a field of the good reads a value
    and the field is a field of a powered product
    and it is not the case that
        the value is a word for no value
    and it is not the case that
        the good has a word of goods of another chapter
    and it is not the case that
        the kind of the good is a kind
    and it is not the case that
        the good is in the shop category a category
        and the category is a shop category of goods of a modelled chapter.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Tests, each from the facts of a ruling or from the listing format
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% Goods of Section XVI by their names: NY J86705 (a plastic switch housing,
% 8538.90), HQ 962145 (a plastic connector housing, 8538.90), NY N313554 (a
% Bluetooth speaker with a rechargeable battery, 8518.21), NY N265396 (a
% power bank, 8507.60), NY N311614 (a smart watch, 8517.62, named in the
% field "Category").
scenario machinery is:
    switch housing 1 is called "switch housing".
    housing 2 is called "electrical connector housing".
    speaker 3 is called "bluetooth speaker".
    the field "power source" of speaker 3 reads "battery".
    bank 4 is called "mobile power bank".
    watch 5 is called "suunto 7".
    the field "category" of watch 5 reads "smart watches".
    the field "is smart device" of watch 5 reads "yes".
    claims expects answers [
        "switch housing 1 is claimed to belong to machinery of section XVI",
        "housing 2 is claimed to belong to machinery of section XVI",
        "speaker 3 is claimed to belong to machinery of section XVI",
        "bank 4 is claimed to belong to machinery of section XVI",
        "watch 5 is claimed to belong to machinery of section XVI"
    ].

% Lamps and furniture: NY 803818 (plastic desk lamps, 9405), NY N239763 (a
% battery LED light string: the lamp claim only, no machinery claim), NY
% I84085 (tables and chairs of resin wicker, 9403 and 9401).
scenario lamps_and_furniture is:
    lamp 1 is called "desk lamp".
    string 2 is called "led light string".
    the field "power source" of string 2 reads "battery".
    table 3 is called "tables".
    chair 4 is called "rocking chair".
    light 5 is in the shop category "lights & lighting".
    the field "voltage" of light 5 reads "220v".
    claims expects answers [
        "lamp 1 is claimed to belong to lighting fittings of heading 9405",
        "string 2 is claimed to belong to lighting fittings of heading 9405",
        "table 3 is claimed to belong to furniture of chapter 94",
        "chair 4 is claimed to belong to furniture of chapter 94",
        "light 5 is claimed to belong to lighting fittings of heading 9405"
    ].

% Chapter 96 and Chapter 90: NY N304395 (plastic ball point pens, 9608.10),
% NY N317961 (a plastic tripod that holds a phone, 9620.00), NY N297982
% (hair clips, 9615), NY N335861 (makeup brushes with ABS handles, 9603),
% NY 882350 (plastic sunglasses, 9004.10).
scenario articles_of_chapter_96 is:
    pen 1 is called "ball point pens".
    stand 2 is called "tripod".
    clip 3 is called "hair clips".
    brush 4 is called "makeup brushes".
    glasses 5 is called "sunglasses".
    holder 6 is called "pen holder".
    claims expects answers [
        "pen 1 is claimed to belong to pens of heading 9608",
        "stand 2 is claimed to belong to tripods of heading 9620",
        "clip 3 is claimed to belong to combs of heading 9615",
        "brush 4 is claimed to belong to brushes of heading 9603",
        "glasses 5 is claimed to belong to instruments of chapter 90"
    ].

% No claim: a heated pullover (NY N287133, 6110.30: Chapter 85 note 1(a)
% excludes electrically warmed clothing) and light-up shoes (NY N341830,
% 6402.99) get their kind from the garments and footwear backgrounds; a toy
% with a battery is in "Toys & Hobbies"; a phone case in "Consumer
% Electronics" has a principal use from the uses background; a listing with
% "Voltage: None" says that it has no voltage.
scenario no_claims is:
    the kind of pullover 1 is pullover.
    the field "power source" of pullover 1 reads "battery".
    the kind of shoe 2 is shoe.
    the field "is electric" of shoe 2 reads "button battery".
    toy 3 is in the shop category "toys & hobbies".
    the field "power source" of toy 3 reads "battery".
    case 4 is in the shop category "consumer electronics".
    the principal use of case 4 is other use.
    part 5 is called "decorative part".
    the field "voltage" of part 5 reads "none".
    the field "power (w)" of part 5 reads "no".
    claims expects answers [].

% Weak evidence that raises a claim: a phone case with a battery (a power
% bank, NY N265396), a plastic part in "Electronic Components & Supplies",
% a good with "Electronic: Yes" and no other word.
scenario weak_evidence is:
    case 1 is called "phone case".
    the principal use of case 1 is other use.
    the field "is electric" of case 1 reads "lithium battery".
    part 2 is in the shop category "electronic components & supplies".
    gadget 3 is called "gadget".
    the field "electronic" of gadget 3 reads "yes".
    claims expects answers [
        "case 1 is claimed to belong to machinery of section XVI",
        "part 2 is claimed to belong to machinery of section XVI",
        "gadget 3 is claimed to belong to machinery of section XVI"
    ].

query claims is:
    which good is claimed to belong to which kind.
